# Walkie-talkie IPC — Clay<->Clod channel. TRACKED as of 2026-08-10 (Tony's
# ruling): git buys Clay read-reach via clone and buys history. It buys ZERO
# insurance against WT-11's failure mode, which is SILENT vanishing —
# recoverability only pays once someone knows to look. So WT-11's whole-file
# convention is untouched by this, and tracking must never be read as licence
# to relax it. Commits are batched AT SEAL, not per dispatch. See WT-14a–d in
# docs/walkieTalkie.md.
genLadder/smoke.fleet.base

#  ⚠ TONY'S DAILY WIP -- NEVER FOR ARCHIVING. Untracked 2026-09-02 after R16's
#  `git add -u` swept both into a commit about the tokenize retirement, so that
#  commit described work it did not contain. Untracking closes the trap
#  STRUCTURALLY: there is nothing left to sweep, and no protected-paths
#  machinery is needed. Working copies are untouched and stay on disk.
#  ⚠ CONSEQUENCE, WRITTEN DOWN BECAUSE OUT-OF-REPO BUILD INPUTS BITE SILENTLY
#  (bear-trap #11's family): a FRESH CLONE RECEIVES NEITHER FILE. Nothing
#  resolves them by path in an executable sense -- checked: no script, manifest,
#  .twk, .rtn or groupIncludes entry, and the Xcode reference is a navigator
#  file-reference only -- but an instrumented build wants a `groupDirectives`
#  to name on tok's command line (bear-trap #23), so create an empty one if you
#  need one. The DEFAULT BUILD IS BARE and never names it.
IncantForms/WorkingOn/incant++
groupDirectives
#  ⚠ tester UNTRACKED 2026-09-01 (SEQ 105, R4). Tony: "my testing incantation, and
#  it will change randomly depending on what I am testing." That is incant++'s exact
#  profile, and a file that churns by design is a standing exception in the
#  cleanliness instrument -- which is the thing nobody re-examines. Untracking it is
#  the same move that let the 09-02 seal drop its "but for Tony's two named files"
#  clause: PREFER A STRUCTURE THAT MAKES THE FAILURE UNCONSTRUCTABLE OVER A
#  DISCIPLINE THAT AVOIDS IT. A dirty tree is a FINDING again.
#  ⚠ UNTRACKED IS NOT UNREAD (Tony, 2026-09-01): Clod looks in on this file when it
#  changes, because it is the cheapest signal of what Tony is working on, and he
#  answers questions about it. It never needs reconciling and is never a finding.
#  ⚠ IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser STAYS TRACKED -- it is WIP with an end date (it
